WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.799
Welcome to Learning How to Learn.

2
00:00:03.799 --> 00:00:06.639
Your brain has amazing abilities,

3
00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.920
but it didn't come with an instruction manual.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.439
Perhaps the greatest gift that our brains give us

5
00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:15.039
is the ability to learn new things every day.

6
00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:18.000
On my way here, I thought about the journey that will take

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.639
us to the last day of the course,

8
00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:22.760
and how much we will learn along the way.

9
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.840
Our goal is to give you a better understanding of how we

10
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.239
learn so that your brain becomes a better learner.

11
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.799
These insights are based on solid research from neuroscience,

12
00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:35.279
from cognitive psychology,

13
00:00:35.279 --> 00:00:37.520
and also from dozens of leading instructors

14
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.439
and practitioners in difficult to learn subjects.

15
00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.680
Whether you're a novice or an expert,

16
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.759
you will find great new ways to improve your skills

17
00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:47.520
and techniques for learning,

18
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.560
especially related to math and science.

19
00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:52.639
This course is meant to help you reframe

20
00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:54.279
how you think about learning,

21
00:00:54.279 --> 00:00:56.439
to help reduce your frustration

22
00:00:56.439 --> 00:00:58.680
and increase your understanding.

23
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.319
We approach things a little differently.

24
00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:04.080
You're not expected to have an in-depth background

25
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.279
in any particular subject.

26
00:01:06.279 --> 00:01:09.000
Instead, you're expected to take these ideas

27
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.080
and apply them to whatever subject

28
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.480
you're trying to learn or improve in

29
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.319
to help you learn more deeply, effectively,

30
00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:18.519
and with less frustration.

31
00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:21.879
You'll hear experts from a variety of different disciplines

32
00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:25.559
talking about their best tips for learning more effectively.

33
00:01:25.559 --> 00:01:27.279
You can benefit from these ideas

34
00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:29.400
whether you are struggling in high school

35
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.559
or soaring through math and science

36
00:01:31.559 --> 00:01:33.720
at graduate levels at a university.

37
00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:38.000
I'm a co-director of a science and learning center

38
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.639
that is sponsored by the National Science Foundation

39
00:01:40.639 --> 00:01:42.599
based here in La Jolla.

40
00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:46.000
In recent years, we've made great strides from research

41
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.279
in discovering how to learn most effectively.

42
00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:51.720
Finding a way to simply and effectively

43
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.519
share these ideas with you has been a big undertaking,

44
00:01:55.519 --> 00:01:57.599
but we feel it's well worth doing.

45
00:01:57.599 --> 00:01:59.440
You'll see that many of these ideas,

46
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.160
although simple, are incredibly powerful.

47
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.440
And along the way, we will also learn a lot

48
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.760
in the process of teaching you.

49
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.600
You'll see how you can fool yourself

50
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.639
about whether you actually know the material.

51
00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:14.160
You'll discover new ways to hold your focus

52
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.600
and embed the material more deeply

53
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.919
and powerfully in your mind.

54
00:02:18.919 --> 00:02:21.160
And you'll learn to condense key ideas

55
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.360
you're learning about so you can grasp them more easily.

56
00:02:24.399 --> 00:02:28.320
Master the simple, practical approaches outlined here,

57
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.720
including simple tips to help prevent procrastination,

58
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.080
and you'll be able to learn more effectively

59
00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.440
and with less frustration.

60
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.960
This course is meant to enrich

61
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.720
both your learning and your life.

62
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.520
You'll be able to get what you want from this material.

63
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.080
So welcome to the course.

64
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.800
And happy learning.